-- title:
--   Eq. (D.1.4.3) — every Hausdorff locally compact abelian group is the directed union (filtered colimit) of its open compactly generated subgroups
-- statement:
--   **Exhaustion by open compactly generated subgroups** (eq. (D.1.4.3) of the source).
--
--   Let $G$ be a Hausdorff locally compact abelian group, and let $\mathrm{CG}(G)$ be the set of all *open compactly generated* subgroups of $G$: the open subgroups $H\subseteq G$ that are generated by a compact neighbourhood of the identity (Definition D.1.4.1 applied to $H$). Then $G$ is the filtered colimit
--   $$G=\operatorname*{colim}_{H\in\mathrm{CG}(G)}H\qquad\text{(D.1.4.3)}$$
--   of these subgroups along their (open) inclusions. Explicitly:
--
--   1. $\mathrm{CG}(G)$ is directed under inclusion: any two members are contained in a third;
--   2. $G=\bigcup_{H\in\mathrm{CG}(G)}H$;
--   3. $G$ carries the colimit topology: a subset $V\subseteq G$ is open if and only if $V\cap H$ is open in $H$ for every $H\in\mathrm{CG}(G)$.
--
--   This is the first step of the structure theory of §D.1.4 of the source. Applied to the dual group $\widehat G$ it yields, by Pontryagin duality, the presentation of $G$ as an inverse limit of locally Euclidean groups (Lemma D.1.4.4); the open compactly generated subgroups $\Gamma\subseteq G$ are also the first components of the structural pairs $(\Gamma,k)$ indexing the inductive limit that defines the Schwartz–Bruhat space $\mathcal S(G)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The set $\mathrm{CG}(G)$ is a variable `CG : Set (Subgroup G)` together with the hypothesis `hCG` that it equals `{H | IsOpen (H : Set G) ∧ ∃ U ∈ 𝓝 1, IsCompact U ∧ Subgroup.closure U = H}`. For an open subgroup `H` this condition says exactly that the topological group $H$ is compactly generated in the sense of Definition D.1.4.1 (such a `U` is contained in `H` and is a compact neighbourhood of the identity of `H`). Directedness is `DirectedOn (· ≤ ·) CG`; in part 3, $V\cap H$ open in $H$ is openness of the preimage of `V` under the inclusion `H → G`.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 758, §D.1.4.1, eq. (D.1.4.3) (with Definition D.1.4.1, p. 757)

import Mathlib

open Topology

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace LCAGroup

theorem openCompactlyGenerated_directed_union
    (G : Type*) [CommGroup G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]
    [T2Space G] [LocallyCompactSpace G]
    (CG : Set (Subgroup G))
    (hCG : CG = {H : Subgroup G | IsOpen (H : Set G) ∧
      ∃ U ∈ 𝓝 (1 : G), IsCompact U ∧ Subgroup.closure U = H}) :
    DirectedOn (· ≤ ·) CG ∧
    (∀ x : G, ∃ H ∈ CG, x ∈ H) ∧
    ∀ V : Set G, IsOpen V ↔ ∀ H ∈ CG, IsOpen ((fun x : H => (x : G)) ⁻¹' V) := by sorry

end LCAGroup
